  "text": "proprium.assumptio-beatae-mariae-virginis-evangelium",
  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit, and cried out with a loud voice, saying, Blessed are you among women and blessed is the fruit of your womb! And how have I deserved that the Mother of my Lord should come to me? For behold, the moment that the sound of your greeting came to my ears, the babe in my womb leapt for joy. And blessed is she who has believed, because the things promised her by the Lord shall be accomplished. And Mary said, My soul magnifies the Lord, and my spirit rejoices in God my Savior; because He has regarded the lowliness of His handmaid; for, behold, henceforth all generations shall call me blessed; because He Who is mighty has done great things for me, and holy is His name; and His mercy is from generation to generation on those who fear Him.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w038", "w039"], "anchor": "w038", "gloss": "came" }, { "words": ["w061", "w062"], "anchor": "w061", "gloss": "were spoken" }, { "words": ["w077", "w078"], "anchor": "w078", "gloss": "in God" }] }
  },
